      },
      "hints": [
        "Substitute $f(x) = \\frac{1}{2}x - 5$ into $g(x) = 3x - 2$.",
        "Expand and simplify."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitute $f(x) = \\frac{1}{2}x - 5$ into $g(x) = 3x - 2$:\n$$gf(x) = g(f(x)) = 3\\left(\\frac{1}{2}x - 5\\right) - 2$$",
        "Expand and simplify:\n$$gf(x) = \\frac{3}{2}x - 15 - 2 = \\frac{3}{2}x - 17$$"
      ]
